      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the remainders when the sum of the three integers is divided by 24. Let's denote the three integers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). According to the problem, we have the following congruences:\n\n\\[a \\equiv 10 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\\[b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\\[c \\equiv 12 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24. First, we add the congruences together:\n\n\\[a + b + c \\equiv 10 + 4 + 12 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the sum on the right-hand side:\n\n\\[10 + 4 + 12 = 26\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[a + b + c \\equiv 26 \\pmod{24}\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 26 is divided by 24. Since 26 is greater than 24, we subtract 24 from 26 to find the remainder:\n\n\\[26 - 24 = 2\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24 is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{2}\\]",
